1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,741
Part five. Leads: every enquiry, followed up.

2
00:00:05,610 --> 00:00:13,752
Every enquiry is a lead, from a call, walk-in, referral, Facebook or your website.

3
00:00:13,752 --> 00:00:17,624
Open CRM, then Leads, and tap New Lead.

4
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:20,247
Type the name and phone.

5
00:00:20,247 --> 00:00:23,037
Add the city, where the lead came from,

6
00:00:23,037 --> 00:00:27,187
the capacity they need and their monthly electricity bill.

7
00:00:27,187 --> 00:00:29,834
These help you plan the right system.

8
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:35,903
Assign it to a sales person and set the next follow-up date and time.

9
00:00:35,903 --> 00:00:40,775
The follow-up appears on the Dashboard and in alerts on that day.

10
00:00:40,775 --> 00:00:41,150
Save.

11
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:48,115
On the lead page, write a note after every call: what was promised, what they asked.

12
00:00:48,115 --> 00:00:52,809
The history keeps every note and change with who did it and when.

13
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:57,564
The WhatsApp button opens a ready message for this lead.

14
00:00:57,564 --> 00:01:02,198
You can change the words, then Open WhatsApp sends you to the chat,

15
00:01:02,198 --> 00:01:04,965
and the message is noted in the history.

16
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:11,807
The Board view shows leads by stage: New, Contacted, Site Visit, Quoted,

17
00:01:11,807 --> 00:01:12,883
Won and Lost.

18
00:01:12,883 --> 00:01:17,268
Move a card to the next stage as the deal progresses.

19
00:01:18,170 --> 00:01:22,884
When the lead is serious, open it and tap Convert to customer.

20
00:01:22,884 --> 00:01:27,750
The customer gets the name, phone, city and state from the lead.

21
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:32,387
You can also go straight to Schedule survey or New quotation.

22
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:37,423
Next video: Customers: one page for everything.

